stion/worked-solution "To work out ${(-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2},$ we multiply $-\\frac{9}{2}$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2} &= (-\\frac{9}{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{2}) \\\\ &= \\frac{9\\cdot 9}{2\\cdot 2} \\\\ &= \\frac{81}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443542 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447ff6ac-8e33-53a7-a4b3-bb9df76bffb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{14},\\,-\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443498} {:answer/id #uuid "6486f987-8f88-59d1-a346-9c83d923a1ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443501} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d0d21b-45e7-55b2-a074-9a46fed29092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443512} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c74af9-8ca2-5cca-a7be-75a239dd9ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443514} {:answer/id #uuid "b7a1952d-4592-5193-b5f8-225ef704bbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7a1952d-4592-5193-b5f8-225ef704bbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443517} :answer-field/id #uuid "de6079b3-a0dd-5241-b8ce-a969c300edc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1147fbce-b0d6-511f-b878-2ccccfbc032b" :question/math-academy-id "q-78437" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\sqrt{6}t,\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=7t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{7}) \\\\  & =⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,2\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\frac{s}{7},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}s}{7},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}s}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0078bb74-f290-5ea7-a214-52b9d695f5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443489} {:answer/id #uuid "90c29a1a-cd28-5b50-b2a0-d5a7e09bc382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443508} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd6f943-95f7-5873-b8a8-4d4dc0f6b355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443518} {:answer/id #uuid "e86fc481-fc66-5c0e-8cd5-654a6782aa39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443528} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb7902b-1060-5a35-9399-e7e8e0a37d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90c29a1a-cd28-5b50-b2a0-d5a7e09bc382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443508} :answer-field/id #uuid "b84fca7e-39f0-5846-a5a5-8d1c1f76b531" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16cdbada-67e8-5de1-a9af-81171c0d9ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-127693" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-3t\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=\\frac{9}{2}{t}^{2}.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parametrization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $y$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=\\frac{9}{2}{t}^{2},$ we have that $t=\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})-3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})+3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})-\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $y$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b22410-7856-5e1a-acc1-6826159d44dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443491} {:answer/id #uuid "1efba70b-6e3e-5b18-88b3-cce733abfbee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443492} {:answer/id #uuid "9b9add6d-7ad1-521a-b998-2bbe4dbdbf01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6s),\\,2-3\\operatorna